  "result": "The 100× overcharge is fixed, and `npm test` passes (9/9). The new tests also pass.\n\n**Root cause:** `buildChargePayload` (`src/payments/gateway/payload.js`) lower-cases the currency for the gateway (`\"JPY\"` → `\"jpy\"`) and then passes that lower-case code to `toMinor`. The currency registry is keyed by upper-case codes, so `jpy` missed the lookup and fell back to the default 2-decimal exponent. ¥1,500 became 150,000. KRW broke the same way. USD and EUR are 2-decimal anyway, so they were unaffected.\n\n**Fix:**\n- `src/payments/gateway/payload.js`: the amount is now computed from the upper-case code. The gateway still receives the lower-case `currency` string.\n- `src/lib/currency/registry.js`: `exponent`, `isSupported` and `symbol` now look codes up case-insensitively, so other callers passing lower-case codes can't hit the same silent fallback.\n\n**Tests added in `test/charge.test.js`:**\n- JPY 1500 gives 1500 and KRW 20000 gives 20000.\n- KWD 1.234 gives 1234.\n- `toMinor(1500, 'jpy')` gives 1500.\n\nI only checked the payment path. Other code that passes lower-case codes into currency lookups, such as the CRM integration, now gets the correct exponent from the registry change, but I didn't audit those callers.",
